### Scenario R: Event Loop Starvation via Synchronous JSON Schema Compilations

* **Domain**: Node.js Event Loop Performance
* **Problem Specification**:
  An MCP server dynamically validates tool inputs against massive OpenAPI specifications (12,000 lines of JSON Schema). Under load (50 concurrent tool calls), the Node.js event loop lag spikes to 850 ms, dropping incoming health check requests.
* **Diagnostic Telemetry**:
  ```bash
  $ node --trace-event-loop-lag dist/server.js
  [EVENT LOOP LAG SPIKE] 842.1 ms at Ajv.compile (node_modules/ajv/dist/core.js:112:14)
  ```
* **Architectural Root Cause**:
  The tool execution handler was compiling Ajv schemas synchronously *on every incoming request* inside the main event loop thread:
  ```typescript
  // Anti-pattern: Compiles schema synchronously on every call
  app.onToolCall((call) => {
    const validate = ajv.compile(massiveSchema); // Blocks event loop!
    validate(call.arguments);
  });
  ```
* **Production Remediation**:
  Pre-compile and memoize all schemas during server startup:
  ```typescript
  export class SchemaValidatorRegistry {
    private compiledValidators = new Map<string, ValidateFunction>();

    constructor(private ajv: Ajv, schemas: Record<string, object>) {
      // Compile ALL schemas once during initialization
      for (const [name, schema] of Object.entries(schemas)) {
        this.compiledValidators.set(name, this.ajv.compile(schema));
      }
    }

    public validate(toolName: string, data: unknown): boolean {
      const validator = this.compiledValidators.get(toolName);
      if (!validator) throw new Error(`Unknown validator: ${toolName}`);
      return validator(data); // Microsecond validation execution
    }
  }
  ```

