## 9. The 20-Point Lead Architect Production Readiness Rubric

Before any enterprise MCP server or multi-agent swarm is promoted to production environments, the lead systems architect must sign off on this comprehensive 20-point readiness rubric:

### Protocol Conformance & Transport
- [ ] **1. Strict Handshake Ordering**: Server rejects all incoming requests prior to receiving `notifications/initialized`.
- [ ] **2. Clean Stream Delimitation**: `stdout` is exclusively reserved for newline-terminated JSON-RPC frames; zero log text.
- [ ] **3. Precise Error Code Mapping**: Errors conform to standard JSON-RPC codes (`-32700` through `-32603`).
- [ ] **4. Protocol Capability Transparency**: All dynamic features (`tools.listChanged`, `resources.subscribe`) are explicitly declared.

### Security & Access Control
- [ ] **5. Ephemeral Workload Credentials**: Infrastructure access relies on temporary STS/App tokens; zero static keys.
- [ ] **6. Hermetic Process Spawning**: Spawned worker sub-processes run with scrubbed, minimal environment variables.
- [ ] **7. AST Database Sanitization**: Dynamic SQL tools parse ASTs and prohibit DDL/destructive operations.
- [ ] **8. Data Loss Prevention (DLP)**: Outbound logs and responses pass through automated secret/PII redaction proxies.

### Concurrency & Resource Governance
- [ ] **9. Deterministic Pipe Draining**: High-volume outputs implement backpressure handling on stream writes.
- [ ] **10. Connection Pool Limits**: Database and HTTP connection pools enforce hard concurrency caps and timeouts.
- [ ] **11. Ephemeral Port Management**: HTTP clients reuse persistent connection pools to prevent `TIME_WAIT` exhaustion.
- [ ] **12. SQLite WAL Lifecycle**: Local state databases configure active checkpoint intervals and busy timeouts.

### Memory & Performance Stability
- [ ] **13. Bounded Deserialization**: Incoming JSON streams enforce maximum nesting depth ($\le 32$) and size limits.
- [ ] **14. Event Emitter Teardown**: SSE transports detach all listeners upon client disconnect to prevent heap leaks.
- [ ] **15. Pre-Compiled Validation Schemas**: JSON schemas are pre-compiled during initialization to eliminate event loop lag.
- [ ] **16. Jittered Rate Limiting**: Retries against upstream enterprise APIs apply full jitter exponential backoff.

### Multi-Agent Coordination & Governance
- [ ] **17. Odd-Numbered Consensus Quorums**: Voting ensembles maintain odd-numbered sizing to prevent split-brain deadlocks.
- [ ] **18. Structured Context Handoffs**: Sub-agents receive compact structured manifests rather than raw conversational logs.
- [ ] **19. Distributed Tracing Propagation**: W3C `traceparent` headers are injected into JSON-RPC `_meta` blocks.
- [ ] **20. Emergency Cascade Kill-Switch**: Central coordinator can terminate all active workers via process group signals.

